==Trivia==
*P.E.K.K.A's name derives from the Finnish name for "''Peter''", which in turn comes from the Greek name "''Petros''", meaning stone.
*The acronym for P.E.K.K.A didn’t officially stand for anything in particular originally. Supercell held a Facebook contest on 22 August 2012 to see who could come up with the best written-out name for P.E.K.K.A as judged by the number of likes the comment received. The name "''Perfectly Enraged Knight Killer of Assassins''" was the winner. The person who submitted the acronym was called Víctor in the [https://www.facebook.com/ClashofClans/photos/478339952190333 Facebook announcement].
*The P.E.K.K.A is 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Witch]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Archer Queen]].
**The P.E.K.K.A resembles the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/P.E.K.K.A Level 1 P.E.K.K.A] from Clash of Clans. Her [[Star Points|Star Level 2 skin]] grants her a second sword similar to the Level 4 P.E.K.K.A in Clash of Clans. However, the P.E.K.K.A in Clash Royale will never attack with the other sword or both swords, while the P.E.K.K.A in Clash of Clans will swing both.
**Like in Clash of Clans, when P.E.K.K.A hits an enemy, a heavy slashing sound effect and a faint, low-pitched laugh plays.
**In Clash of Clans, the P.E.K.K.A's movement speed is moderate whereas in Clash Royale, her movement speed is low.
*The P.E.K.K.A is one of the first troop [[cards]] to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the Minions, Archers, Knight, [[Spear Goblins]], Goblins, [[Bomber]], Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], Witch, [[Prince]], and Balloon.
*The P.E.K.K.A is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, Prince, Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, Cannon Cart, [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], Lava Hound, [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The P.E.K.K.A is 1 of 10 troops that has been featured under the [[Ruler Ability#Special Delivery|Special Delivery]] [[Ruler Ability|ruler ability]], the others being Knight, Skeleton Barrel, Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Wizard, Giant Skeleton, Golem, [[Sparky]], and Royal Ghost.
*The P.E.K.K.A is 1 of 23 cards that has had its [[Elixir]] cost changed, the others being Bomber, [[Fire Spirit]], Royal Recruits, [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], Musketeer, [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], Skeleton Army, Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], Bowler, [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], Fisherman, and the [[Monk]].
**The P.E.K.K.A, the Cannon, and the Mortar were the first cards whose Elixir cost was changed since the [[Version History#February 2016 Update (2/2/2016)|February 2016 Update]].
*The P.E.K.K.A is 1 of 3 troops that has had its Melee range classification changed, the others being Mini P.E.K.K.A and Giant.
**The P.E.K.K.A is the first troop whose Melee range classification was changed since the 5/8/2019 balance changes.
*The P.E.K.K.A is 1 of 15 troops which bring an excited reaction from the audience upon spawning and brings a collective groan from the audience when defeated, as well as a concerning gasp when the opponent plays her, the others include [[Royal Giant]], Giant, Giant Skeleton, [[Rune Giant]], Goblin Giant, Golem, Bowler, [[Electro Wizard]], [[Inferno Dragon]], Sparky, Lava Hound, Night Witch, [[Super Lava Hound]], and the Monk.
*The P.E.K.K.A's gender has been confirmed as female, as one of the Loading Screen Hints in Clash of Clans states, ''"The armor on P.E.K.K.A is so heavy that Spring Traps don't affect her"'', and also several videos from the official YouTube. In Clash Royale, the P.E.K.K.A. Protector [[Battle Banners|decoration]]'s description says "''No one messes with her butterfly''".
**However, in the Arabic, Persian, and Finnish language setting of the game, the P.E.K.K.A is referred to as male, according to her card description.
*According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=BRING-YOUR-CHILD-TO-WORK-DAY_Final.jpg strip], the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]] is the P.E.K.K.A's child.
*There is a [[Loading Screen Hints|Loading Screen Hint]] that says: ''"P.E.K.K.A: No one knows what's behind that mask. Maybe even another mask.".'' This is a reference to the anime [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naruto Naruto], specifically the episode called: "''[https://naruto.fandom.com/wiki/Gotta_See!_Gotta_Know!_Kakashi-Sensei's_True_Face! Gotta See! Gotta Know! Kakashi-Sensei's True Face!]''"
*The P.E.K.K.A may be a reference to [https://backyardmonsters.fandom.com/wiki/D.A.V.E. D.A.V.E.] from [https://backyardmonsters.fandom.com/wiki/Backyard_Monsters_Wiki Backyard Monsters]. Both have names that don't stand for anything in particular, both are robotic in nature and both were considered the strongest regular troop in their respective games.
*The P.E.K.K.A is featured as a [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Hero_Skins?file=PEKKA_King_info.png skin for Barbarian King in Clash of Clans].
*The P.E.K.K.A's sword can be seen can be seen on the [[Trophies|Trophy Road]] as a decoration.
*The P.E.K.K.A is featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The P.E.K.K.A, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, and [[Elite Barbarians]], were featured as a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Monster monster] in [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Puzzle_%26_Dragons_Wiki Puzzles and Dragons], in a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Dungeon dungeon] called [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Clash_of_Clans_Dungeon Clash of Clans Dungeon].
**The P.E.K.K.A, along with the Goblins, Barbarians, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, and the Archer Queen, were featured as a non-playable opponent in [https://www.chess.com/ Chess].
**The P.E.K.K.A is featured as [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Ash?file=Ash_Skin-P.E.K.K.A.S.H.png a character skin for Ash] in Brawl Stars.
**The P.E.K.K.A, along with the Minions, Bomber, Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, [[Mega Minion]], [[Ice Golem]], Dart Goblin, Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Guards]], Baby Dragon, Giant Skeleton, Golem, Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, [[Inferno Dragon]], Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The P.E.K.K.A has a passion towards butterflies. Her passion for butterflies is also referenced a few times:
**When deployed, the P.E.K.K.A will briefly say ''"Butterfly"'' in a deep robotic voice.
***The P.E.K.K.A. is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being Mini P.E.K.K.A., Mega Minion, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Dark Prince]], Bowler, [[Ram Rider]], [[Electro Wizard]], [[Princess]], Ice Wizard, Magic Archer, [[Lumberjack]], [[Mother Witch]], Fisherman, [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Boss Bandit]], Archer Queen, [[Little Prince]], and the [[Terry]].
**In Clash of Clans, every day, a butterfly will spawn near the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Trader Trader]. If an [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Army_Camp/Home_Village Army Camp] housing a P.E.K.K.A is nearby, a P.E.K.K.A will chase after it, saying "''Butterfly''" in a raspy robotic voice. She sounds upset when the butterfly despawns.
**In the Clash of Clans [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fYpB24pIU_8 P.E.K.K.A. commercial] where the P.E.K.K.A chases a butterfly.
**The P.E.K.K.A. Protector Decoration's description saying "''No one messes with her butterfly''".
**{{Trait|P.E.K.K.A.}} is represented by a butterfly icon.
*There is an [[Arenas|Arena]] based on the P.E.K.K.A called P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse, which shares the name of a [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Single_Player_Campaign#P.E.K.K.A's_Playhouse Single Player Map] in Clash of Clans.
*The P.E.K.K.A is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically: 
**The P.E.K.K.A is the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The P.E.K.K.A is the subject of a few [[Emotes]].
**The P.E.K.K.A is the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].
**The P.E.K.K.A is the subject of a few Battle Banner items.
***The P.E.K.K.A is one of the first troops to be the subject of a Battle Banner item, along with the Mini P.E.K.K.A, Dart Goblin, Prince, Giant Skeleton, Mega Knight, [[Super Witch]], and the Golden Knight.
***The P.E.K.K.A Protector decoration is identical to its card render.
***The Night of the Living P.E.K.K.A frame is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_of_the_Living_Dead Night of the Living Dead]. Its description says "''They're coming to get you, Barbarian!''", which is also a reference to the same film.
*The P.E.K.K.A was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/DVY2TndGf4U?si=ptuVz0tHkkkDIvEl Crown Championship Global Series Tournament], by a player called Sergioramos:).
*The initial balance change for P.E.K.K.A on the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (5/8/2019)|5/8/2019 balance changes]] was a 15% hitpoints decrease, but it was lowered to 9.5% [https://x.com/Seth_Supercell/status/1158324991684988928?s=20 last minute].
*The P.E.K.K.A is said to be piloted by a spirit trapped inside of the armor, as seen in a [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FSZHXlHyrZM short].
**A popular theory shown in the video is that there was a 5th spirit, the Nature spirit, who was rejected by the King for being too weak when discovered by him. The Nature Spirit would become upset and remain dormant near an old suit of armor until fusing with it and becoming the P.E.K.K.A.
**In "[[w:c:clasharama:Clash-A-Rama!|Clash-A-Rama!]]", in the episodes [https://youtu.be/aUnB5nzmmtc?si=yrXyrKdPlfez__d2&t=436 12 Days of Clashmas] and [https://youtu.be/7mPbPLbVfoc?si=eqHqdxpikzgQojwJ&t=579 Clone Alone], it's shown that the P.E.K.K.A has a phonograph or DJ set inside and is sometimes piloted by the Mini P.E.K.K.A.
***The Zap Evolution lore [https://youtu.be/Rtgpx2YLLO4?si=AvAMV3xPB1KHwPtK short] also shows the Mini P.E.K.K.A inside.
*In the "[https://youtu.be/Qo0Innwk2FY?si=HqNUzg0LmohA_DF9&t=43 Clash-A-Rama! Tower Decoration!]" video, it's shown that the P.E.K.K.A. can fire lasers from her eyes.

